cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TriMedAI: code and results"
message: >-
  The article this repository accompanies is under review and not yet
  published. Please cite the article rather than the repository once it
  appears; the entry under preferred-citation gives its details.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NinniSingh1991/trimedai"
abstract: >-
  Simulator, agents, comparators and analysis code for a hidden-parameter
  Markov decision process that decides when an assistive system should summon
  a caregiver. Activity context is recognised from the UCI Human Activity
  Recognition corpus under a subject-wise split; the care process above it is
  simulated, so nothing here is evidence about clinical performance.
keywords:
  - assistive technology
  - cooperative inverse reinforcement learning
  - reinforcement learning
  - meta-learning
  - hidden-parameter Markov decision process
  - escalation timing
  - simulation study
